Report the text path's three silent failures.

Upstream's text path fails and returns quietly in three places. On a desktop that is a
fair trade - the font is installed, so a message nobody will read is noise. In a port it
is the wrong one, because whether the font arrived is the open question:

  - `font_load` never checks `TTF_OpenFontRW`. A size that fails to open leaves a null
    `ttf[i]`, `font_load` still returns 1, and every later string at that size renders as
    nothing.
  - `font_load` returns 0 for a missing file and for a failed open alike.
  - `make_image_from_font` drops a failed `TTF_RenderUTF8_Blended` on the floor, under a
    comment reading "Pretend everything's just fine". A glyph that was never rendered then
    looks exactly like one rendered and sampled wrong - opposite problems, same symptom.

**Only the calls are here.** The reporting - the format strings, the counters, the throttle
on the render failure, the summary - is `shim/nb_diag.c`, and `shim/include/nb_diag.h` says
why. Two reasons, the second decisive: a patch is rebased onto every upstream revision and
shim code is not, and this archive compiles with `-w`, so a format string written into it is
checked by nobody and a bad one faults rather than warns on this target. Every entry point
takes strings and an int, so this patch cannot get an argument list wrong - it never writes
one.

`nb_diag_report()` is not here either. The shim already wraps `main`, so the summary goes
after that call returns and `ball/main.c` stays untouched.

Nothing here counts textures, draws or GL errors. oops-gl sees every one of those without a
call site and reports them itself - `tex-created`, `tex-failed`, `gl-errors`, `draws-*` -
which is why this is twelve added lines and not two hundred.

